  "id": "listening-strategy",
  "term": "listening strategy",
  "definition": "A listening strategy is the way a person approaches and organizes what they hear when trying to make sense of speech. In this source, it refers especially to whether someone listens in a more discrete, category-based way or a more gradient, flexible way, with the latter helping more in difficult, noisy speech settings.",
